# CODEOWNERS — review gate on the privacy walls.
#
# Every path here is load-bearing for a privacy guarantee (Docs/Verifiability.md): the wall
# tests, the wall scripts and hooks, the CI workflow that enforces them, the documents that
# state them, the package manifest whose dependency DAG *is* the S3 wall, and the privacy
# manifests the App Store shows users. With branch protection's "Require review from Code
# Owners" enabled (Docs/Release-Process.md), no change to these files can merge without the
# owner's explicit approval — a wall cannot be weakened in a drive-by commit.
#
# Deliberately narrow: ordinary feature code is NOT listed, so this gate cannot rot into a
# rubber stamp. If a path is added here, say in the PR why it is wall-load-bearing.
#
# Every pattern must resolve to an existing file or directory —
# Tests/FernletTests/CodeOwnersResolutionTests.swift enforces it, so a restructure that moves
# a protected file fails CI instead of silently unprotecting the wall (which is exactly what
# the 2026-08-12 App/+Tests/ restructure did to 11 of the 26 entries here).

